  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public Financial Management in Ghana&apos;s Health Sector project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Supplier shall be responsible for delivery of the following outputs to the Ghana Health Service (as part of the Ministry of Health and working alongside the Ministry of Finance), subject to their confirmation. These outputs relate to the Ghana Health Service but can be extended to other service providers as applicable and practically possible.  1. Enhanced health sector knowledge, application and compliance with Public Financial Management law and regulations.2. Increased capacity on budget preparation and execution.3. Improved budget transparency and accountability throughout all stages of the budgeting process e.g. how budgets are managed and presented at a Regional and District level.4. Strengthened use of financial data for informed decision-making by the Ghana Health Service and to improve their resource prioritisation.5. Improved governance and engagement in health budget preparation and monitoring at the community level.</narrative>
  </description>
